dir/.yo
description: Directory with the control .yo subdirectory - the overlays live under it
- >
  A dir carrying the hidden control subdirectory `.yo/`. The directory itself becomes a yamlover
  NODE, and the overlays add what bare disk cannot say:
- !!<format: text/plain> |
  .yo/
    body.yo      - the INSTANCE overlay: data values over the directory
    meta.yo      - the METADATA schema: types, formats, presentation
    settings.yo  - project configuration (the served root only)
    index.db     - engine cache (derived)
    fragments/   - image crops a body key points at (derived)
    thumbnails/  - preview renderings of a blob member (derived)
    .trash/      - storage of DETACHED members, kept recoverable
- >
  `body.yo` is the instance overlay - a scalar SELF-VALUE for the directory, extra keyed fields
  no file holds, references, bookmarks and back-edges, and ORDER: its positional pointer-array
  (`- *file1 ...`) grants positions to the children it names, and disk has none - this is exactly
  what lifts the plain dir's no-lists and no-scalar limits. `meta.yo` is the metadata schema -
  types, formats, decoding, what turns a file's bytes into a value. Either overlay is optional,
  and the mere presence of `.yo/` is the marker that promotes the concrete.
- >
  The overlay subtree is HIDDEN, not secret: `body.yo`, `meta.yo` and the index cache are read by
  the engine and never appear as entries, while `settings.yo` and the two sidecar directories ARE
  indexed - hidden from the table of contents, yet addressable (`*:.yo:settings.yo`,
  `*:.yo:thumbnails:cover.png`). `.trash/` alone is skipped ENTIRELY - a deleted member leaves the
  projection while its storage survives here, recoverable. Nothing else may live under `.yo/` - see the
  [layout invariants](*::language:concretes:02-invariants). The storage-wide rules live in
  [the storage axis](*::language:concretes:00-storage) and the
  [choosing rules](*::language:concretes:01-choosing).
